        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "648eac79-b761-588e-a0a2-b1e8581495eb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: George McCall Theal, August Frederik Beutler, Everhardus Cornelis Godée Molsbergen\n- Places: Saint John, New Brunswick, Bay of Fundy, Cape Town, Wynberg\n- Roles: historian, archivist, genealogist\n- Topics: South African historiography, expedition accounts, publication history\n\nFacts:\n- George McCall Theal was born on 11 April 1837 in Saint John, New Brunswick, and died on 17 April 1919 in Wynberg, Cape Town.\n- Saint John is a port city on the Bay of Fundy in the Canadian province of New Brunswick.\n- George McCall Theal was the most prolific and influential South African historian, archivist, and genealogist of the late nineteenth and early twentieth century.\n- August Frederik Beutler wrote a comprehensive account of his pioneering expedition.\n- George McCall Theal first published August Frederik Beutler’s expedition account in 1896.\n- The Dutch historian Everhardus Cornelis Godée Molsbergen, who lived from 1875 to 1940, published August Frederik Beutler’s expedition account in 1922.",
